{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f2b1c40-6c1e-4f2a-9c1b-2b7d5a9e4c10",
    "name": "Advani Family Office — Internal Dashboard API",
    "description": "Every endpoint on the internal dashboard API.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. Import `advani-dashboard.postman_environment.json` and select it.\n2. Point `baseUrl` at your API (`http://localhost:4000/api` or the Vercel URL).\n3. Send any request.\n\nThere is no sign-in step to perform by hand. A collection-level pre-request script notices that no `accessToken` is set, requests an OTP for `email`, reads the code straight out of the response (email delivery is disabled on this deployment, so the API returns it), verifies it, and stores the token pair. Every other request inherits bearer auth from the collection.\n\nTo sign in as somebody else, change `email` and clear `accessToken`.\n\n## Roles\n\nUnder open signup the first account to sign in becomes ADMIN and everyone after that becomes EDITOR. To exercise the RBAC failures, set a user to VIEWER via `PATCH /users/{id}/role`, then sign in as them and try a write — the API answers 403.\n\nList requests capture the first row's id into a collection variable (`assetId`, `investmentId`, and so on), so the detail, update and delete requests below them work without copying ids around.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Signs in on demand, so no request in this collection needs a manual token.",
          "const path = pm.request.url.getPath();",
          "",
          "// The auth and health endpoints must not trigger a sign-in of their own.",
          "if (path.indexOf('/auth/') !== -1 || path.indexOf('/health') !== -1) {",
          "  return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')) {",
          "  return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "const baseUrl = pm.environment.get('baseUrl') || pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
          "const email = pm.environment.get('email') || pm.collectionVariables.get('email');",
          "",
          "const json = (body) => ({",
          "  mode: 'raw',",
          "  raw: JSON.stringify(body),",
          "  options: { raw: { language: 'json' } },",
          "});",
          "",
          "console.log('No access token — signing in as ' + email);",
          "",
          "pm.sendRequest(",
          "  {",
          "    url: baseUrl + '/auth/request-otp',",
          "    method: 'POST',",
          "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
          "    body: json({ email: email }),",
          "  },",
          "  (otpError, otpResponse) => {",
          "    if (otpError) {",
          "      console.error('Could not reach the API: ' + otpError);",
          "      return;",
          "    }",
          "",
          "    const challenge = otpResponse.json();",
          "",
          "    if (!challenge.devCode) {",
          "      console.error(",
          "        'The API did not return a code, so EXPOSE_OTP is off. Set accessToken by hand.',",
          "      );",
          "      return;",
          "    }",
          "",
          "    pm.sendRequest(",
          "      {",
          "        url: baseUrl + '/auth/verify-otp',",
          "        method: 'POST',",
          "        header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
          "        body: json({ email: email, code: challenge.devCode }),",
          "      },",
          "      (verifyError, verifyResponse) => {",
          "        if (verifyError) {",
          "          console.error('Could not verify the code: ' + verifyError);",
          "          return;",
          "        }",
          "",
          "        const session = verifyResponse.json();",
          "        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', session.accessToken);",
          "        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', session.refreshToken);",
          "        pm.collectionVariables.set('currentUserId', session.user.id);",
          "        console.log('Signed in as ' + session.user.email + ' (' + session.user.role + ')');",
          "      },",
          "    );",
          "  },",
          ");"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000/api", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "reviewer@advanifamilyoffice.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "currentUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "assetId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "investmentId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "transactionId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "distributionId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "filingId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
